@style(IDocDemo)
@title(Figures and media)

Pictures, figures with captions, video, PDF pages, icons, diagrams and shapes.

@section(Pictures and figures)

@subsection(@@img)

An image.

@img(src=circuit.svg, caption=Front)
@draw(caption=Plan)
…
@end
@end
@figure(src=circuit.svg, caption=Measured response, label=fig-r, alt=A circuit)

@img(file=circuit.svg, w=60%)

@img(file=circuit.svg, inline)

@img(circuit.svg, w=200, h=120, fit=contain, alt=A series circuit, label=fig-circ, gap=12px)

@img(circuit.svg, w=140, float=right, alt=Circuit floating right)
Text runs beside a floating picture. It keeps going here so the wrap is visible on screen.

@img(circuit.svg, w=140, float=left, alt=Circuit floating left)
And here the picture floats left.

Turned and cropped: @img(circuit.svg, w=160, rotate=90, alt=Rotated circuit) @img(circuit.svg, w=200, crop=10% 0 10% 5%, alt=Cropped circuit) @img(circuit.svg, scale=0.5, alt=Half size)

@subsection(@@figure)

A NUMBERED figure with a caption, referenceable with ref, placed where it is written.

@figure(file=circuit.svg, caption=Result, label=fig1)

@figure(caption=Three views, cols=3)

@figure(file=circuit.svg, span)

@figure(src=circuit.svg, alt=A battery and two resistors in series, caption=A series circuit, columns=1)

@figure(src=circuit.svg, w=50%, alt=A series circuit at half width, caption=Half width)

@subsection(@@icon)

A built-in icon glyph, sized and coloured like text.

@icon(check)

@icon(warning, size=2em)

@subsection(@@shape)

A vector shape: rect, ellipse, triangle, diamond, pentagon, hexagon, star, arrow, line, callout.

@shape(star, w=80, fill=#f5b800)

@shape(arrow, x=20%, y=40%)

@section(Video and PDF)

@subsection(@@video)

A video player.

@video(file=clip.mp4, width=60%, poster=circuit.svg)

@video(src=clip.mp4, label=A short test clip, loop, stage, w=360)

@video(src=clip.mp4, autoplay, w=240)

@subsection(@@pdf)

A PDF in the document.

@pdf(file=datasheet.pdf)

@pdf(file=datasheet.pdf, w=70%, caption=The brief)

@pdf(file=datasheet.pdf, edit)
pages 1-3
highlight 1 10%,20%,60%,3%
note 1 at 80%,10% "Read this first" id=n1
note 1 at 84%,10% "Done: see page 2" reply=n1 by="TA"
fill student.name="Ada Lovelace"
export datasheet.pdf
@end

@pdf(file=datasheet.pdf, h=40vh, alt=A one-page lab data sheet)

An editing exercise on the same PDF: @pdf(file=datasheet.pdf, edit, expect=pages=1, pts=2, id=pdf-ex1)

@pdf(file=datasheet.pdf, edit, noedit, id=pdf-ex2)

@section(Diagrams)

@subsection(@@diagram)

A figure that is computed, not drawn: give the measures and it is solved and drawn to scale, varies with rand, prints as vector, is described for screen readers, and ask= turns its unknown into a graded blank with a computed answer.

@diagram(triangle, a=5, b=7, C=40, ask=c, units=cm)

@diagram(symbol, resistor, style=iec)

@diagram(circuit, series, V=9, R1=2k, R2=1k, ask=I)

